  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25598414",
      "title": "Adding a Users List Component",
      "sourceHash": "c302abeec6a7cebefd50eee8a35a9a88101525e6e535c0c1ef979731d687f861",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.56,
          "end": 7.26,
          "en": "So let's tackle our list of users next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 7.26,
          "end": 10,
          "en": "Now the first important question is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10,
          "end": 11.72,
          "en": "where do we wanna output?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.72,
          "end": 15.3,
          "en": "And the second question that depends on the first one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.3,
          "end": 19.89,
          "en": "is where we then actually wanna manage our list of users?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.89,
          "end": 22.52,
          "en": "So where do we wanna output that list?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.52,
          "end": 26.29,
          "en": "We get the user data here in the AddUser component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.29,
          "end": 30.35,
          "en": "and technically we could simply add more HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.35,
          "end": 33.25,
          "en": "in that component to all the render a list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.25,
          "end": 36.17,
          "en": "maybe here unordered list below the form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.17,
          "end": 40.13,
          "en": "We could then manage our list of users with use state in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.13,
          "end": 43.72,
          "en": "here in AddUser and output it down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.72,
          "end": 45.36,
          "en": "That is something we could do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.36,
          "end": 48.45,
          "en": "and technically that would absolutely work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.45,
          "end": 50.3,
          "en": "But by the way, I'm saying this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.3,
          "end": 53.75,
          "en": "you already hear that this is probably not how we're going",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.75,
          "end": 55.36,
          "en": "to do it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.36,
          "end": 58.21,
          "en": "The idea in React really is that you work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.21,
          "end": 59.61,
          "en": "with a bunch of components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.61,
          "end": 62.181,
          "en": "that you have small isolated pieces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.181,
          "end": 66.48,
          "en": "of HTML code and logic where every component really",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.48,
          "end": 68.01,
          "en": "has its own task,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.01,
          "end": 71.67,
          "en": "its own responsibility you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.67,
          "end": 73.02,
          "en": "And therefore you wanna keep",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.02,
          "end": 76.76,
          "en": "your components small and focused.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.76,
          "end": 79.28,
          "en": "You could certainly argue that a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.28,
          "end": 80.85,
          "en": "that fetches user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.85,
          "end": 84.44,
          "en": "and then outputs this as a list is focused enough",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.44,
          "end": 86.81,
          "en": "but I would argue that it's better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.81,
          "end": 90.38,
          "en": "to have one component that fetches user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.38,
          "end": 93.56,
          "en": "that's this AddUser component which we already have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.56,
          "end": 96.65,
          "en": "And then we have another component that is responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.65,
          "end": 98.6,
          "en": "for outputting the list of users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.6,
          "end": 101.35,
          "en": "so that we split the outputting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.35,
          "end": 104.663,
          "en": "and the fetching logic into two different components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.58,
          "end": 107.71000000000001,
          "en": "And therefore I'll add a brand new component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.71000000000001,
          "end": 112.71000000000001,
          "en": "the UsersList component, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.92,
          "end": 116.55,
          "en": "And here the UsersList component should be responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.55,
          "end": 119.033,
          "en": "for well, outputting my user data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.1,
          "end": 121.57,
          "en": "Therefore, in there, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.57,
          "end": 123.39,
          "en": "we're going to write a React component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.39,
          "end": 125.32,
          "en": "So let's import React from React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 125.32,
          "end": 127.6,
          "en": "so that we can use JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.6,
          "end": 129.313,
          "en": "And then here we have UsersList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.5,
          "end": 134.24,
          "en": "We get our props here and we'll of course export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.24,
          "end": 137.763,
          "en": "our component here so that we can use it in our files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.47,
          "end": 143.47,
          "en": "And then here I want to in the end return an unordered list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.47,
          "end": 146.78,
          "en": "where I want to go through a list of users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.78,
          "end": 149.7,
          "en": "which I well, need to get in some way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.7,
          "end": 153.21,
          "en": "and output a couple of list items for every user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.21,
          "end": 155.65,
          "en": "So one list item for every user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.65,
          "end": 157.06,
          "en": "How does this work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.06,
          "end": 159.84,
          "en": "Well, it think it makes sense to assume",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.84,
          "end": 161.98,
          "en": "that in the UsersList component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.98,
          "end": 166.98,
          "en": "we rely on props to get our actual array of users as data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.89,
          "end": 169.9,
          "en": "So here between the unordered list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.9,
          "end": 172.68,
          "en": "we could actually use props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.68,
          "end": 174.42000000000002,
          "en": "Let's say users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.42000000000002,
          "end": 175.73,
          "en": "it's your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.73,
          "end": 179.3,
          "en": "So it's up to you which prop name you expect here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 179.3,
          "end": 183.36,
          "en": "I expect to have a prop property which is named users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.36,
          "end": 186.87,
          "en": "and that should hold an array of user data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 186.87,
          "end": 189.04,
          "en": "So we can use the map method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.04,
          "end": 192.81,
          "en": "which you learned about in the lists and conditionals module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.81,
          "end": 196.19,
          "en": "to map that array of users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.19,
          "end": 199.4,
          "en": "queue and array of JSX elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.4,
          "end": 202.74,
          "en": "So to transform our user data to JSX elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.74,
          "end": 205.92000000000002,
          "en": "which then are rendered onto the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.92000000000002,
          "end": 209.21,
          "en": "So map executes a function on every item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.21,
          "end": 210.71,
          "en": "in the user's array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 210.71,
          "end": 213.14,
          "en": "and we'll get that item as input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.14,
          "end": 214.73,
          "en": "Since it's an array of users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.73,
          "end": 217.24,
          "en": "I'll name that single item user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.24,
          "end": 219.94,
          "en": "and write a anonymous arrow function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 219.94,
          "end": 222.29,
          "en": "And then in this anonymous arrow function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.29,
          "end": 225.65,
          "en": "we return a JSX element for every user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 225.65,
          "end": 229.113,
          "en": "of that user's array we expect to get on this prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 230.48,
          "end": 231.66,
          "en": "So the element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 231.66,
          "end": 233.67000000000002,
          "en": "the JSX element which I wanna render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 233.67000000000002,
          "end": 235.78,
          "en": "is simply a list item here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 235.78,
          "end": 238.04,
          "en": "and inside of the list item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 238.04,
          "end": 240.69,
          "en": "I want to output the username.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 240.69,
          "end": 243.42,
          "en": "Let's say we expect user to be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 243.42,
          "end": 245.21,
          "en": "with a name property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 245.21,
          "end": 247.22,
          "en": "then we could do it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 247.22,
          "end": 248.71,
          "en": "And then thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 248.71,
          "end": 250.32,
          "en": "maybe in parentheses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 250.32,
          "end": 252.19,
          "en": "and that's just text here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 252.19,
          "end": 253.89,
          "en": "not a special react syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 253.89,
          "end": 256.57,
          "en": "So between this parentheses text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 256.57,
          "end": 261.103,
          "en": "I want to output let's say user.age years old.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 262.34,
          "end": 265.47,
          "en": "So my expectation here is that users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 265.47,
          "end": 267.94,
          "en": "is an array of user objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 267.94,
          "end": 272.173,
          "en": "where every object has a name property and an age property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 273.1,
          "end": 275.62,
          "en": "Why can I expect this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 275.62,
          "end": 278.15,
          "en": "Because we're the ones creating this app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 278.15,
          "end": 281.4,
          "en": "It's up to us to decide how we wanna manage our data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 281.4,
          "end": 284.1,
          "en": "And I wanna manage an array of user objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 284.1,
          "end": 287.683,
          "en": "where every object has a name property and age property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 288.99,
          "end": 293.183,
          "en": "So with that we have the logic in place to output our users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 294.04,
          "end": 296.02,
          "en": "Some styling would be nice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 296.02,
          "end": 297.01,
          "en": "And for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 297.01,
          "end": 300.03,
          "en": "I first of all will wrap this list in a card.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 300.03,
          "end": 303.2,
          "en": "So I want to have that card component look here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 303.2,
          "end": 308.2,
          "en": "So I'll import card again from UI card",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 308.27,
          "end": 309.87,
          "en": "and we need to import it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 309.87,
          "end": 313.09,
          "en": "even though we already imported it in AddUser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 313.09,
          "end": 315.76,
          "en": "because you need to import what you wanna use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 315.76,
          "end": 318.48,
          "en": "in a certain component into every component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 318.48,
          "end": 320.02,
          "en": "where you wanna use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 320.02,
          "end": 322.81,
          "en": "So it's not enough to just import card once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 322.81,
          "end": 325.48,
          "en": "in another component you need to import it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 325.48,
          "end": 328.203,
          "en": "in every component where you wanna use the card.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 329.15,
          "end": 333.62,
          "en": "With that we can use card here to wrap the unordered list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 333.62,
          "end": 336.12,
          "en": "And now I also wanna have some styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 336.12,
          "end": 341.06,
          "en": "And for that you find a UsersList.module.css file attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 341.06,
          "end": 344.88,
          "en": "which you can just drag and drop into your users folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 344.88,
          "end": 349.24,
          "en": "And from there, you know the game we can import classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 349.24,
          "end": 354.24,
          "en": "from UsersList.module.css to use that CSS modules feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 357.21,
          "end": 358.39,
          "en": "And then here on the card,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 358.39,
          "end": 360.41,
          "en": "I'll add the class name prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 360.41,
          "end": 362.94,
          "en": "which I can because a few lectures ago,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 362.94,
          "end": 364.57,
          "en": "we made sure that we utilize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 364.57,
          "end": 368.55,
          "en": "the incoming class name prop here instead of the card.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 368.55,
          "end": 369.86,
          "en": "So we can set it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 369.86,
          "end": 373.73,
          "en": "We can set the prop and I set it to classes.user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 373.73,
          "end": 377.55,
          "en": "to have not just a default card class on that card component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 377.55,
          "end": 379.713,
          "en": "but also my special user class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 381.17,
          "end": 383.74,
          "en": "Excuse me, users not user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 385.53,
          "end": 388.16,
          "en": "With that we got a UsersList component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 388.16,
          "end": 389.63,
          "en": "Now we need to use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 389.63,
          "end": 391.41,
          "en": "And that leads us to the next question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 391.41,
          "end": 394.593,
          "en": "Where do we wanna use this brand new component?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 395.54,
          "end": 397.86,
          "en": "We could use it here in AddUser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 397.86,
          "end": 401.81,
          "en": "We could use it here below to form UsersList like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
